   140	\paragraph{Tool-Use Learning.}
   141	Toolformer \cite{toolformer-2024} inserts API calls via self-supervised filtering; ART \cite{art-2023} delegates tool selection to reasoning chains; Chameleon \cite{chameleon-2024} composes modules under LLM-as-planner orchestration; ReTool \cite{retool-2026} uses RL for implicit code-interpreter invocation. These methods learn \emph{which tool} to use but do not analyze what signal drives routing. We generate labels via episode-level counterfactual analysis, revealing ${\sim}90\%$ is death avoidance.
